  "answer_markdown": "The stages of an ingestion `Pipeline` are as follows, with the required stages marked. The `TypeError` you encounter is likely due to a missing required argument in one of these stages [1][3]:\n\n1. **`FileLoader` (Required)** – Reads raw bytes from a source (e.g., `FilesystemFileLoader`). This stage is mandatory as it provides the input data for the pipeline [1][3].\n\n2. **`DocumentExtractor` (Required)** – Converts the `File` into a structured `Document` (e.g., `PlainTextExtractor` or `MistralOCRExtractor` for PDFs). This stage is mandatory to parse the raw content [1][3].\n\n3. **`TextSplitter` (Required)** – Divides the `Document` into smaller `DocumentChunk` objects (e.g., `CharacterTextSplitter`). This stage is mandatory to prepare chunks for embedding [1][3].\n\n4. **`DocumentProcessor` (Optional)** – Adds metadata to chunks (e.g., `SummaryEnricher` or `ChunkEnricher`). This stage is optional and can be omitted [1][3].\n\n5. **`Embedder` (Required)** – Converts each chunk into a vector (e.g., `MistralEmbedder`). This stage is mandatory for indexing [1][3].\n\n6. **`stores` (Required)** – Persists the vectors and raw text in a vector store (e.g., Vespa). This stage is mandatory to index the chunks [1][3].\n\n### Example of a Valid Pipeline Initialization\nTo avoid a `TypeError`, ensure all required arguments are provided. Here is a working example from the documentation [1][3]:\n\n```python\npipeline = Pipeline(\n    loader=FilesystemFileLoader(),  # Required\n    extractor=PlainTextExtractor(),  # Required\n    text_splitter=CharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=512),  # Required\n    processors=[],  # Optional (can be empty)\n    embedder=MistralEmbedder(client=mistral_client, model_name=MODEL_1024_EMBEDDING),  # Required\n    stores=vector_store,  # Required\n)\n```\n\nIf you are missing a required argument (e.g., `loader`, `extractor`, `text_splitter`, `embedder`, or `stores`), the `Pipeline` will raise a `TypeError`. Double-check that all required components are initialized and passed correctly [1][3].",
