  "answer_markdown": "Agentic Search requires the index to be a **`NavigableIndex`**, specifically configured with `IndexingMode.DOCUMENT_PER_CHUNK` to preserve source offsets and enable chunk navigation in reading order [2]. This setup allows the model to inspect documents, move between chunks, and exclude already-seen content during retrieval loops [2].\n\nThe navigation tools exposed by Agentic Search include:\n\n- **`search(query, top_k, exclude_ids)`**: Runs semantic or hybrid retrieval across the collection, avoiding previously inspected chunks via `exclude_ids` [2].\n- **`open(source_id, start_offset, end_offset, window)`**: Expands context around a retrieved chunk by returning adjacent chunks in reading order [2].\n- **`navigate(source_id, start_offset, end_offset, direction, top_k)`**: Steps forward or backward through a document from a known position [2].\n- **`read(source_id, start_offset, end_offset, top_k)`**: Reads chunks from a specified source range [2].\n- **`grep(source_id, pattern, mode, top_k)`**: Performs lexical search for exact terms or phrases within a single document [2].\n- **`ingest(uri)`**: Adds a document (local path, `file://`, or `http(s)://` URI) to the index [2].\n- **`delete(source_id)`**: Removes a document and all its chunks from the index [2].",
